<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<subsection xml:id="course_prerequisites" label="course_prerequisites" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Course Prerequisites</title>
  <p>
    A grade of C or better in MATH 4083 is required to enroll in this course.
  </p>
  <p>
    In particular, students are expected to have experience with the following topics.
    <ul>
      <li>
	<p>
	  arithmetic in the integers, such as
	  <ul>
	    <li>division with remainder,</li>
	    <li>greatest common divisors and the Euclidean algorithm,</li>
	    <li>the Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic,</li>
	    <li>congruence modulo <m>n</m> and <m>\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}</m></li>
	  </ul>
	</p>
      </li>
      <li>
	<p>
	  rings, such as
	  <ul>
	    <li>the ring axioms and their basic consequences,</li>
	    <li>integral domains, fields, units, and zero divisors,</li>
	    <li>subrings and Cartesian products,</li>
	    <li>ring homomorphisms and isomorphisms</li>
	  </ul>
	</p>
      </li>
      <li>
	<p>
	  ideals and quotient rings, such as
	  <ul>
	    <li>kernels and ideals,</li>
	    <li>ideals generated by elements,</li>
	    <li>quotient rings,</li>
	    <li>the canonical decomposition and the First Isomorphism Theorem,</li>
	    <li>the Chinese Remainder Theorem,</li>
	    <li>the Third Isomorphism Theorem</li>
	  </ul>
	</p>
      </li>
      <li>
	<p>
	  linear algebra, such as
	  <ul>
	    <li>linear independence and spanning sets,</li>
	    <li>bases,</li>
	    <li>dimension</li>
	  </ul>
	</p>
      </li>
      <li>
	<p>
	  groups, such as
	  <ul>
	    <li>the group axioms, subgroups, and group homomorphisms,</li>
	    <li>cyclic groups and orders of elements,</li>
	    <li>group actions,</li>
	    <li>symmetric, alternating, and dihedral groups,</li>
	    <li>cosets, normal subgroups, and quotient groups,</li>
	    <li>the isomorphism theorems for groups</li>
	  </ul>
	</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</subsection>
